Pyro patch 0043: WindowProxy and Location refuse prototype changes and non-extensibility.

HTML's Location object and the cross-origin Window and Location objects keep their prototype
([[SetPrototypeOf]] is SetImmutablePrototype) and refuse [[PreventExtensions]]; a WindowProxy
refuses [[PreventExtensions]] too. JavaScript cannot give a callback object or the global proxy
those internal methods.

kJSClassAttributeImmutablePrototype (JSForkPrivate.h) gives a JSClass's wrappers both:
Object.setPrototypeOf to anything but the current prototype throws (Reflect.setPrototypeOf is
false) and Object.preventExtensions throws (Reflect.preventExtensions is false).
JSObjectSetPrototype still sets their prototype for the embedder (a cross-origin object's null).
JSGlobalContextSetGlobalProxyRefusesPreventExtensions marks a context's global proxy as a
WindowProxy, which then refuses [[PreventExtensions]] whichever global it reaches.

